An extra `}` inside a DoProc argument list: the second `}` is stray, the
`)` still closes the call. Reported once as unmatched_delimiter, not
mismatched_delimiter (diag.unmatched_delimiter second Flags fence).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE QueueLabel;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nCopies;
	:DECLARE vResult;
	vResult := DoProc("PrintLabelCopies", {sSampleId, nCopies}});
	:RETURN vResult;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE PrintLabelCopies;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nCopies;
	:RETURN nCopies;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE QueueLabel;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nCopies;
	:DECLARE vResult;
	vResult := DoProc("PrintLabelCopies", {sSampleId, nCopies}});
	:RETURN vResult;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE PrintLabelCopies;
	:PARAMETERS sSampleId, nCopies;
	:RETURN nCopies;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:60-4:61 error unmatched_delimiter: Unmatched '}'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:60-4:61 error unmatched_delimiter: Unmatched '}'
9:14-9:23 hint unused_variable: Variable 'sSampleId' is declared but never used
